@startuml 13-deployment-diagram
title Intended deployment topology — LibraFlow

skinparam defaultFontName "Tahoma"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam node {
  BackgroundColor #EAF2F8
  BorderColor #34495E
}
skinparam cloud {
  BackgroundColor #F7F9F9
  BorderColor #85929E
}

node "ผู้ใช้" as CLIENT {
  artifact "Web Browser" as BROWSER
}

cloud "Vercel" as VERCEL {
  artifact "React SPA\nhttps://library-book-management-alpha.vercel.app" as FRONTEND
}

cloud "Render" as RENDER {
  artifact "Spring Boot API\nhttps://library-book-management-ybt2.onrender.com" as BACKEND
}

cloud "Neon" as NEON {
  database "PostgreSQL\nDatabase: libraflow" as DB
  artifact "Branch shown in supplied screenshot: production" as NEON_BRANCH
}

cloud "GitHub" as GITHUB {
  artifact "Repository branches\nmain = production\ndevelop = integration/test" as REPO
  node "GitHub Actions" as CI {
    artifact "Backend: Maven clean verify\nFrontend: npm ci, lint, build, audit" as CHECKS
  }
}

BROWSER --> FRONTEND : HTTPS 443
BROWSER --> BACKEND : HTTPS 443 / REST + JWT
BACKEND --> DB : JDBC over TLS
NEON_BRANCH -- DB
REPO --> CI : push / pull request

note right of REPO
  Intended release flow:
  personal branch -> PR -> develop -> review -> main
  develop is the test/integration branch.
end note

note bottom of RENDER
  Configure production Render service to track main.
  The connected branch and deployed commit are not
  verifiable from the public service URL.
end note

note bottom of DB
  Render DB_URL selects the Neon branch/database.
  Neon having a branch called production does not
  prove that Render connects to that branch.
end note

note bottom of CI
  CI validates code; this workflow does not deploy.
  Verify Render and Vercel Git settings in their dashboards.
end note

@enduml
